# The cast and the art layout (phase 1, cast lane, 2026-11-08)

Settles spec 2.2, 3, 5.2 and 8 for `packs/cast/cast.js`, `tools/build_art.py` and the art manifests. Read this
instead of the code. Tests: `node --test "tests/cast.test.cjs"`.

## 1. `BBCast` (packs/cast/cast.js)

A UMD file: the page gets `window.BBCast`; Node gets it from `require('packs/cast/cast.js')`. It is data plus one
pure helper.

```
BBCast = {
  version: 1,
  people: { <id>: { name, art, role, scale?, who, voice, tts: { voices, pitch, rate },
                    twin?, short?, exact?, newest?, tipScale?, threeStarScale? } },
  poses: { customer: [10 names], manager: [10 names], promoted: 'promoted', extra: ['neutral'] },
  drawn(BBArt.cast) -> [ids]
}
```

- **id** is the art folder name (spec 2.2) and matches `/^\w+$/`. **art** is that same id, or `null` for someone with
  no picture (`pa`, and the generic `shopper` speaker).
  - A person's poses are `packs/cast/art/cast/<art>/<pose>.webp`.
  - A shopper's one picture is `packs/court/art/shoppers/<art>.webp`.
- **role** is one of:
  - `manager`: `mitch`.
  - `regular`: `marge gus bev vernon sal` (every restaurant), and `dale priya oakes tasha` (some restaurants, spec 5.4).
  - `visitor`: `reginald kai`.
  - `local`: `tony pam` (pizza), `breeze brock` (smoothie), `jitters` (cafe), `hiro dennis` (sushi), `inferno rita`
    (burrito), `lulu walt` (icecream).
  - `voice`: `pa`, the mall announcer.
  - `extra`: `shopper1`…`shopper6` (pictures), plus `shopper`, the speaker id for `court.chatter` (captions only).
- **Which restaurants someone visits is not in the cast.** Each pack's `regulars` lists them (spec 8). The spec 5.4
  table is the contract; tests/cast.test.cjs keeps a copy of it.
- **scale**: `kai` 0.74 and `lulu` 0.66. Every other character leaves it out (draw at 1). All poses share one tall
  canvas, so a child drawn at `scale` keeps their feet on the floor line: scale from the bottom centre.
- **name** is what captions and `{name}` show: "Coach Bev", "Professor Oakes", "Chef Hiro", "Little Lulu",
  "Grandpa Walt", "Announcer", "Shopper".
- **who / voice** are the briefs from DESIGN.md's cast table and `art-source/jobs/write_prompts.py`. `voice` is the brief
  for the final voice pass. None of them leans on accent or background.
- **Traits** are persona fields, copied from the Burger Bar (tests check them against `tests/packs/diner-golden`):
  - `gus`: `twin: true`, `tipScale: 1.25`
  - `vernon`: `exact: true`, `threeStarScale: 1.5`
  - `reginald`: `newest: true`
  - `kai`: `short: true`
  
  Nobody else has a trait. What anyone orders (likes, usual, dislikes, favourite) belongs to the pack.
- **poses** lists the pose names from spec 2.2. `promoted` belongs to plain `mitch` only.
- **drawn(BBArt.cast)** returns the ids, in cast order, of customers (regular, local or visitor) whose folder has every
  customer pose. The page can pass this to `S.create(pack, { drawn })` (spec 4.5).
- **Mitch's art**:
  - `people.mitch.art` is `'mitch'`: Mitch in his shirt and tie. That folder has the ten poses plus `promoted`, for the
    grand celebration.
  - Each restaurant dresses him through `pack.manager.art`: `mitch-burger` for the diner, `mitch-<pack>` everywhere
    else.
  - All seven uniform folders have all ten poses now.

## 2. Text to speech

**Choosing the voice.** `js/audio.js` (`pickVoice`, the audio lane's) does the choosing, reading `BBCast.people[id].tts`:

- The first fragment in `tts.voices` that matches a device voice wins. Case doesn't matter, and the match must start a
  word.
- If none matches, a stable hash picks a voice, skipping the player's scan voice.

**How the lists are ordered.** Each list starts with an Edge natural voice: Guy, Aria, Jenny, Christopher, Roger, Ryan,
Sonia, Natasha and so on. After that come the hub's Windows voices. Every list reaches David, Mark or Zira, so on the
hub nobody is left to the hash.

**Windows rounds pitch and rate to whole steps.** On the hub's Electron, Chromium sends SAPI
`<pitch absmiddle="trunc(pitch*10-10)">` and `SetRate(trunc(10*log10(rate)))`. Here `rate` is the player's rate times
the character's. I measured all six voices on this PC with SAPI, through the same markup:

- **A pitch step is only about half a semitone.** Zira runs 137 to 242 Hz over the whole -10..+10 range, and David
  barely moves.
- **A rate step is about 11% of length.**
- **Rates from 0.8 to 1.25 are all step 0.** So the old diner values (pitch 0.7 to 1.25, rate 0.88 to 1.12) made almost
  no audible difference.

The recipes are chosen to fit that:

- Each value sits well inside its step: 0.88 is -1, 1.12 is +1, 1.32 is +3. Rates 0.9 to 1.12 are step 0, 1.3 and up
  are +1, and 0.77 and down are -1.
- Speakers who can meet at a restaurant, or at the court, and end up on the same voice must be far enough apart. On this
  PC's six voices, and on a PC with only David, Zira and Mark, that means one of:
  - 3 pitch steps apart;
  - 2 pitch steps and a rate step;
  - 2 rate steps.
- They also stay at least 2 pitch steps (or a pitch step and a rate step) apart when the player's own rate is 0.8 or
  1.25.
- A level-4 cameo (any other restaurant's local) is also at least 2 pitch steps (or a pitch step and a rate step) apart.
- Nobody sits on the game's own voice (pitch step 0 and rate step 0).
- No two speakers share a pitch and rate anywhere.
- Mitch keeps today's 1.15 / 1.12.
- Pitch stays within 0.48 to 1.72 and rate within 0.75 to 1.45, so Edge's smooth voices still sound human.
- On a fresh PC with only David and Zira, there are no exact clashes, but some pairs are only a step apart. That case is
  not required.

| id | voices (preference order) | pitch | rate | SAPI steps (pitch, rate) | this PC (6 voices) | David/Zira/Mark only |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| mitch | Guy, Mark, David | 1.15 | 1.12 | +1, 0 | Mark | Mark |
| marge | Michelle, Zira, Susan, Hazel | 1.12 | 0.9 | +1, 0 | Zira | Zira |
| gus | Christopher, David, Mark | 0.48 | 1.05 | -5, 0 | David | David |
| bev | Aria, Susan, Zira, Hazel | 0.48 | 1.08 | -5, 0 | Susan | Zira |
| vernon | Ryan, George, Mark, David | 1.52 | 0.92 | +5, 0 | George | Mark |
| sal | Andrew, David, Mark | 0.78 | 1.3 | -2, +1 | David | David |
| dale | Davis, Brian, Mark, David | 0.88 | 0.75 | -1, -1 | Mark | Mark |
| priya | Sonia, Susan, Zira, Hazel | 0.88 | 1.34 | -1, +1 | Susan | Zira |
| oakes | Steffan, George, Mark, David | 1.32 | 1.35 | +3, +1 | George | Mark |
| tasha | Emma, Hazel, Zira, Susan | 0.88 | 0.77 | -1, -1 | Hazel | Zira |
| reginald | Thomas, George, Mark, David | 0.68 | 0.9 | -3, 0 | George | Mark |
| kai | Jenny, Zira, Hazel | 1.42 | 1.05 | +4, 0 | Zira | Zira |
| tony | Roger, David, Mark | 1.42 | 0.95 | +4, 0 | David | David |
| pam | Ava, Zira, Susan | 1.62 | 1.36 | +6, +1 | Zira | Zira |
