The shoppers have recipes too, but `court.chatter` is never spoken.

**Changing a recipe.** Edit it, then run `node --test "tests/cast.test.cjs"`.

**Adding a cameo** (spec 2.2):

- tests/cast.test.cjs already checks every possible cameo pairing.
- Any pack's `regulars` are also added to that restaurant's group when the pack loads.
- So a cameo that a content agent adds is checked for real.

## 3. The art layout

| Source (art-source/) | Output | Treatment |
|---|---|---|
| `cast/<id>/<pose>.png` | `packs/cast/art/cast/<id>/<pose>.webp` | BiRefNet cut-out, white fringe removed, the whole 768×1152 canvas, q88 |
| `cast/shopper<N>/neutral.png` | `packs/court/art/shoppers/shopper<N>.webp` | cut out, 3/8 scale (384×576), cropped to the figure: the bottom edge is the feet, and every shopper is at one scale |
| `backdrops/{counter,grill,board}.png` | `packs/diner/art/backdrops/<name>.webp` | 1536×1024, sharp, q86 |
| `backdrops/<pack>-<name>.png` | `packs/<pack>/art/backdrops/<name>.webp` | the same (`diner-fryer` becomes the diner's `fryer`) |
| `backdrops/court.png` | `packs/court/art/court.webp` | 1536×1024, sharp, no blur, q90 |
| `props/{shutter,grandOpening,goldSign,progressBoard}.png` | `packs/court/art/props/<name>.webp` | cut out, cropped, at most 640 px, q90 |
| `props/<pack>-<name>.png` | `packs/<pack>/art/props/<name>.webp` | a restaurant's own version of a shared prop (none yet) |
| any other `props/<name>.png` | `packs/shared/art/props/<name>.webp` | register, bell, back5, spatula, ticketWheel |

**Phase 1 copied and never moved.**

- `packs/diner/art/cast/*` were copied to `packs/cast/art/cast/` and `packs/diner/art/props/*` to
  `packs/shared/art/props/`. The copies are byte-identical, with the same dates.
- The old folders stay until the coordinator deletes them in phase 3. build_art never writes into them.

## 4. Manifests

Each manifest is a UMD script that sets `BBArt.<key>` in the page and `module.exports` in Node.

```
BBArt.cast    = { people: { <folder>: [poses] }, castSize: [768, 1152] }        packs/cast/art/manifest.js
BBArt.shared  = { props: [names] }                                               packs/shared/art/manifest.js
BBArt.court   = { picture: true|false, pictureSize: [1536, 1024], props: [names],
                  shoppers: { shopper1: [w, h], ... }, shopperScale: 0.375 }     packs/court/art/manifest.js
BBArt[<pack>] = { backdrops: [names], props: [own prop names], backdropSize: [1536, 1024] }
                                                                                 packs/<pack>/art/manifest.js
BBArt.diner   = { cast, backdrops, props, castSize, backdropSize }               packs/diner/art/manifest.js
```

- **`BBArt.cast.people`** has a folder for every character and for every Mitch uniform (`mitch-burger` … `mitch-icecream`).
  Not every folder has every pose. Code follows the list: `BBCast.drawn` decides which customers come in, and a missing
  uniform pose falls back to that folder's `neutral` (spec 2.2).
- **`BBArt.court.shoppers`** gives each shopper's cropped pixel size, all at one scale. To draw them in proportion, use
  `height = h × k` with one `k` for all six.
- **`BBArt.court.picture`** is false when court.webp is missing. Then the page draws the storefronts itself (spec 3).
- **`BBArt[<pack>].props`** lists only that restaurant's own versions of shared props. Look up a prop like this:
  1. `packs/<pack>/art/props/<name>.webp` when `BBArt[pack].props` has it;
  2. else `packs/shared/art/props/<name>.webp` (court props: `packs/court/art/props/`).
- **`BBArt.diner` keeps today's shape**, key for key:
  - `cast` and `props` still list the old `packs/diner/art/{cast,props}`, which stage.js reads until the page switches
    over. Under the new rule its `props` are "diner overrides" that are the same pictures as the shared ones.
  - `backdrops` now also has `fryer` and `drinks`.
  - Once phase 3 deletes the old folders, the next build_art run empties `cast` and `props`.

## 5. Re-running build_art

From the game folder:

```
"%USERPROFILE%/Documents/WSD-Art-Tools/ComfyUI/.venv/Scripts/python.exe" tools/build_art.py [ids...] [--dry] [--force]
```

- **It is incremental.** An output newer than its source is skipped. A run with nothing new never loads BiRefNet or uses
  the GPU.
- **Each run rewrites every manifest from what is on disk.** A manifest file is only touched when its text changes.
- **It checks names.**
  - A source with no rule (a backdrop without a restaurant prefix, a pose name with a dash, an unknown folder) is warned
    about and skipped.
  - A source it can't read yet, because it is still being written, is skipped and picked up next time.
- **What it prints:**
  - each file it built;
  - `built N of M`;
  - which manifests changed;
  - "still to draw in art-source/cast", which lists missing poses against spec 2.2.
- **`ids`** limits the run to those cast folders or shoppers. Backdrops and props are still brought up to date.
- **`--dry`** lists what it would build and writes nothing. **`--force`** rebuilds everything.
- After a run, check with `node --test "tests/cast.test.cjs"`. The manifest tests compare every list with the files on
  disk.

## 6. index.html

The `<!-- cast: ... -->` block, just before `js/save.js`, loads:

- `packs/cast/cast.js`;
- the cast, shared and court manifests;
- the art manifests of pizza, smoothie, burrito, cafe, sushi and icecream.

The diner's manifest is already loaded further up. The page agent keeps the block. Every file it names exists: in
dom-play, a missing script counts as a jsdom error.
